id: pm-gok2km
title: "GH-969: brief item reads can exceed standard output because omission receipts bill empty fields"
description: The brief get/show projection can emit more bytes than standard because full restore hints are added for empty or default-valued fields that were cheaper to render. Preserve omission honesty while making depth cost monotone and agent-predictable.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,context-efficiency,output-contracts,token-budget
created_at: "2026-08-10T22:59:19.233Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T23:08:11.446Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Brief output never exceeds standard output for the same item and format; Empty or default-valued omissions do not incur a larger receipt than the value they replace; Property and integration tests cover monotone brief standard deep and full projection costs without hiding material omissions
parent: pm-5t33or
reporter: GitHub issue #969
severity: medium
environment: pm 2026.8.10 CLI get/show depth projections
repro_steps: "Create a small item with comments and notes, then compare byte counts for show --depth brief, standard, deep, and full."
expected_result: Projection depth is monotone in emitted cost while every material omission remains discoverable.
actual_result: Brief measured 1400 bytes versus 1313 bytes for standard because restore hints cost more than empty body and unclaimed state.
affected_version: 2026.8.10
component: CLI output projections
regression: false
customer_impact: Agents cannot trust the low-context depth control and spend more context while requesting less.
